@model bool
@* #221 / D18: the three permission states, one copy, every pre-sitting host.
   `Model` is `promptable`: true on a settings or pre-sitting screen, false inside a sitting.
   A sitting surface may report what the browser decided but may never offer a control that asks. *@
<div class="audio-equipment__permission" data-permission-state="never-asked" hidden>
  <div class="alert alert--warning audio-equipment__perm-box" role="status">
    <strong>Microphone permission: not asked yet.</strong>
    <span class="audio-equipment__perm-text">
      This browser has not been asked for your microphone. Nothing has been refused — ask once here and the answer is remembered for this browser.
    </span>
  </div>
  @if (Model)
  {
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm btn--primary mt-2" data-audio-action="request-permission">
      Enable the microphone to see device names
    </button>
  }
</div>

<div class="audio-equipment__permission" data-permission-state="denied" hidden>
  <div class="alert alert--danger audio-equipment__perm-box" role="alert">
    <strong>Microphone permission: blocked.</strong>
    <span class="audio-equipment__perm-text">
      You refused this site the microphone — or dismissed the prompt without answering. Nothing you do on this page can undo that; the block is held by the browser.
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="audio-equipment__remedy mt-2">
    <p class="text-sm no-margin audio-equipment__remedy-lead"><strong>How to unblock it, in your own browser:</strong></p>
    @* The browser is detected at render time by audio-gate.js; the panel it prints names the exact
       control path for that browser and no other. A generic "allow the microphone" sentence is the
       defect this block exists to prevent. *@
    <div class="audio-equipment__browser" data-denied-browser="chrome">
      <p class="text-sm no-margin">Chrome: click the <strong>tune</strong> icon at the left of the address bar, choose <strong>Site settings</strong>, set <strong>Microphone</strong> to <strong>Allow</strong>, then reload this page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="audio-equipment__browser" data-denied-browser="edge" hidden>
      <p class="text-sm no-margin">Edge: click the <strong>lock</strong> icon at the left of the address bar, open <strong>Permissions for this site</strong>, set <strong>Microphone</strong> to <strong>Allow</strong>, then reload this page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="audio-equipment__browser" data-denied-browser="firefox" hidden>
      <p class="text-sm no-margin">Firefox: open <strong>Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Permissions → Microphone → Settings…</strong>, remove the block for this site, then reload this page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="audio-equipment__browser" data-denied-browser="safari" hidden>
      <p class="text-sm no-margin">Safari: open <strong>Safari → Settings for This Website → Microphone</strong> and choose <strong>Allow</strong>, then reload this page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="audio-equipment__browser" data-denied-browser="opera" hidden>
      <p class="text-sm no-margin">Opera: click the <strong>camera/microphone</strong> icon at the left of the address bar, choose <strong>Site settings</strong>, set <strong>Microphone</strong> to <strong>Allow</strong>, then reload this page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="audio-equipment__browser" data-denied-browser="unknown" hidden>
      <p class="text-sm no-margin">Open this site's permissions in your browser's address bar or settings, set <strong>Microphone</strong> to <strong>Allow</strong>, then reload this page.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted no-margin mt-1">
      After you change it, this page still reads "blocked" until you reload — browsers only re-read the permission on a fresh page load.
    </p>
  </div>
  @if (Model)
  {
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm mt-2" data-audio-action="retry-permission">
      I changed it — check again
    </button>
  }
</div>

<div class="audio-equipment__permission" data-permission-state="granted" hidden>
  <div class="alert alert--success audio-equipment__perm-box" role="status">
    <strong>Microphone permission: granted.</strong>
    <span class="audio-equipment__perm-text">This browser has allowed the microphone for this site. The device list below is now readable.</span>
  </div>
</div>

@* #221 / D18: names are withheld by the browser until permission is granted, so an empty list means
   two different things. These two panels say which; "no devices found" for both is the state the
   product shipped before this ticket. *@
<div class="alert alert--warning mt-2" data-audio-role="device-hint-labels" hidden>
  <strong>Device names are withheld until the microphone is enabled.</strong>
  The browser hides every label behind the permission prompt. Enable the microphone above, then the list fills in.
</div>
<div class="alert alert--warning mt-2" data-audio-role="device-hint-connect" hidden>
  <strong>No microphone is connected.</strong>
  Plug in a headset or a microphone — the permission is fine, there is simply no device to record from.
</div>
